# Response headers for the static site. Cloudflare reads this from the built
# assets directory, and everything in public/ is copied there verbatim.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is NOT here. Astro emits it per page as a meta
# element containing a hash of every script and style it bundled, which a
# hand-written header cannot do without going stale on the next build. Two
# policies would both apply and the stricter would win per directive, so a
# second one here would only ever break things. See `security.csp` in
# astro.config.mjs.
#
# Deliberately absent: Strict-Transport-Security. HSTS is the one header here
# that is genuinely hard to take back — browsers honour it for its full
# max-age whatever you serve afterwards — so it should be a decision made on
# purpose rather than inherited from a config file.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # frame-ancestors is ignored inside a meta element, so framing is refused
  # here instead. No page on this site has any business being framed.
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  # Nothing here uses any of them.
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()

# Fingerprinted filenames, so they can be cached permanently: Astro puts a
# content hash in the name, and a change produces a new URL rather than a
# stale cache.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
